
Structural design patterns deal with how classes and objects are composed to form larger 
structures while keeping the system flexible and loosely coupled.

They focus on organizing relationships between objects rather
than creating them.

Purpose
-------

- Simplify object relationships
- Reduce coupling
- Reuse existing classes
- Build flexible and scalable systems

Memory Trick
------------

Creational  → How objects are CREATED.

Structural  → How objects are CONNECTED.

Behavioral  → How objects COMMUNICATE.

